WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:10.400
Hey you, welcome to Chat With Traders. This is&nbsp;
Tessa, episode 314 and it's the last one of 2025.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.520
This episode is stripped down. No guests,&nbsp;
no experts, no intro outro music. It's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.400
not a recap of 2025, and it's definitely not a&nbsp;
forecast for 2026. My co-host Ian is off traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:33.200
somewhere beautiful. So today, it's just me and&nbsp;
you. And yes, I am a real human being. I have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.000
say this because believe it or not, I still&nbsp;
occasionally hear from listeners who thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.800
I was AI when I first started co-hosting.&nbsp;
I promise. Beating heart, real voice. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:55.280
how are you? How was your 2025? Did it fly by so&nbsp;
fast you didn't even have time to reflect? If so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.240
you're definitely not alone. For those who don't&nbsp;
know, I've been trading for over 10 years, though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:06.800
of course not the whole time, but definitely had&nbsp;
my share of losses like many people. Honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:13.760
it wasn't until Ian and I took over hosting the&nbsp;
podcast in the summer of 2022 that I truly got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:20.320
serious about trading. How could I not? On one&nbsp;
side, we're constantly talking to incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:27.680
talented traders. On the other, we're surrounded&nbsp;
by a community of traders, strivers, builders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:36.880
people putting in the work every single day to&nbsp;
make it in trading. I know because I was there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.600
with some of you in the accountability calls when&nbsp;
we had the Chat With Traders Community platform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:52.320
a few years ago. Together we opened up, became&nbsp;
vulnerable and shared our struggles, frustrations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:02:00.400
but we also showed our hard determination, our&nbsp;
persistence. So, how could I not take trading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:07.680
more seriously since then? If you've ever achieved&nbsp;
consistency or success, maybe this episode is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.360
reminder of where you once were. If you're just&nbsp;
starting out, maybe it offers a glimpse of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:21.680
comes next. But if you're in the middle like I&nbsp;
am, what I'm sharing may really speak to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:30.560
You know, the middle is a strange place. You're&nbsp;
not new or a beginner trader anymore, but you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.800
not where you want to be yet either. You know, we&nbsp;
don't talk enough about what the stage actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:46.560
feels like, like what's confusing or what's&nbsp;
quietly changing in our journey? What progress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:53.760
looks like when it doesn't show up on a chart or&nbsp;
in our P&amp;L? Have you ever felt the discomfort and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:03:00.880
wondered, "Am I still doing something wrong? Or&nbsp;
is this exactly what I'm supposed to be feeling?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:07.360
You know, the idea for this episode actually&nbsp;
came from an unexpected place. My little niece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:13.760
introduced me to a beautiful song called&nbsp;
"What It Sounds Like" from a very famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:21.520
kids animated movie called K-pop Demon Hunters.&nbsp;
Obviously, that K-pop song is not about trading,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:29.040
but it resonates so deeply because there are so&nbsp;
many parallels to the song with trading. Maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:35.680
listen to it and you'll know what I mean. The song&nbsp;
isn't loud. It doesn't resolve the way you expect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:44.160
It's more about awareness than answers. It starts&nbsp;
with ... "Nothing but the truth now..."  When I hear that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:51.760
I think of the journaling that reveals our real&nbsp;
stats and patterns. Maybe the patterns in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:58.800
habits that we're ashamed of. We try to fix it to&nbsp;
force the discipline even though we might not yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:06.800
be aligned internally. But the broken glass in&nbsp;
the song are like the big drawdowns and blown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:14.880
accounts and the painful lessons that become&nbsp;
the scars that can actually strengthen us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:23.040
There's even a line in the song about listening to&nbsp;
the demons, not fighting them, not silencing them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:29.760
just noticing when they start to get between us.&nbsp;
And I realize that's exactly what the stage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:35.680
trading feels like to me. When I think about&nbsp;
where I am as a trader and where a lot of you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:43.280
probably are too, I keep coming back to the same&nbsp;
idea. What the middle actually sounds like. We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:51.040
not blowing up anymore, but we're not confident&nbsp;
either. We're aware enough to feel this gap and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:58.560
feel that something is changing in our journey,&nbsp;
but from the outside, nothing may seem different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:08.000
but internally things are quietly shifting. We&nbsp;
hear hesitation earlier. We feel risk differently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:14.000
We notice when we're forcing trades and when a&nbsp;
voice starts to sound a little too convincing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:20.560
Others might think we're not trading enough.&nbsp;
Our P&amp;L doesn't tell the whole story anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:26.320
There's a moment in that song where nothing&nbsp;
really resolves. And that's what the stage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:32.960
of trading feels like to me. We're not lost, but&nbsp;
we're not done. We're learning how to recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:39.840
when things are working, even when it doesn't&nbsp;
feel good yet. There's no graduation moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:50.640
no breakthrough trade, but we just keep showing&nbsp;
up, heads down, grinding, refining. THIS is what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:58.800
the middle sounds like... From Ian and me at Chat&nbsp;
with Traders, thank you for being here this year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:05.040
Thank you for your listenership. Wherever you're&nbsp;
heading into 2026, especially if you're still in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:12.480
the middle, we wish you clarity, patience, and&nbsp;
a great start to the year ahead. Thank you.

